@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Notice";
}

<div class="govuk-width-container">
    <div class="govuk-grid-row">
        <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
            <h1 class="govuk-heading-l">
                Privacy Notice
            </h1>

            <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">
                Heat Network Technical Assurance Scheme (HNTAS) Digital Platform
            </h2>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                The Energy Act 2023 enables regulations to require heat networks to meet minimum technical standards, with legislation expected by 2027 following DESNZ consultation. The Heat Network Technical Assurance Scheme (HNTAS) will support compliance through regulated technical codes and assurance processes. Independent assessors will verify compliance at design, construction, and operational stages, leading to certification. A digital service is needed to manage compliance, assessment, and certification data effectively.
            </p>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                This notice sets out how we will use your personal data, and your rights. It is made under Articles 13 and/or 14 of the UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR).
            </p>

            <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">Your data</h3>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                We will process the following personal data:
            </p>

            <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
                <li>Names, email and phone number of applicants involved in preparing and submitting Heat Network assessments</li>
                <li>Names and contact details of assessors involved in review and approval of Heat Network assessments</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">1. Purpose</h2>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                We process your personal data for the purposes of administering the HNTAS service, including user registration, organisation onboarding, submission and assessment of technical and compliance information, and, where necessary, in connection with audit, assurance activity, or legal challenge.
            </p>

            <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">2. Legal basis of processing</h2>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                The legal basis for processing your personal data is provided under the UK GDPR Article 6(1)(e): processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in DESNZ. This includes the exercise of statutory and administrative functions, including those conferred by legislation, and the delivery of regulatory, assurance and compliance activities.
            </p>

            <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">3. Recipients</h2>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                We may share your data with government departments, regulators and trusted service providers where necessary to run the HNTAS service. We may also share it if required by law, for example to prevent fraud or comply with a court order.
            </p>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                As part of our IT infrastructure, your personal data will be stored in the UK on systems provided by our data processor - Amazon Web Services. This does not mean we actively share your personal data with these entities; rather, they are technical service providers who host infrastructure supporting our IT systems.
            </p>

            <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">4. Retention</h2>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                We keep data for up to 15 years because heat networks are long-term infrastructure, and we may need to review records for audit, regulatory or legal purposes many years after they were created.
            </p>

            <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">6. International transfers</h2>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                Your data will be processed in the UK.
            </p>

            <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">7. Your rights</h2>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                You have the right to request information about how your personal data are processed, and to request a copy of that personal data.
            </p>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                You have the right to request that any inaccuracies in your personal data are rectified without delay.
            </p>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                You have the right to request that any incomplete personal data are completed, including by means of a supplementary statement.
            </p>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                You have the right to request that your personal data are erased if there is no longer a justification for them to be processed.
            </p>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                You have the right in certain circumstances (for example, where accuracy is contested) to request that the processing of your personal data is restricted.
            </p>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                You have the right to object to the processing of your personal data where it is processed for direct marketing purposes.
            </p>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                You have the right to object to the processing of your personal data.
            </p>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                To exercise your rights please contact the Data Protection Officer using the contact details below.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
